{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun unusually bright. He sat up in bed, a strange stiffness in his limbs, and glanced around his room. It was… too perfect. The furniture was arranged with an unnatural symmetry, the colors vibrant and almost cartoonish. A notification box floated in his vision: \"Welcome to Aethelgard! Level 1 reached. Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone from the Goblin Caves.\" He stared, dumbfounded, at the shimmering text. A nearby mirror reflected not his familiar, slightly weary face, but a younger, more sculpted version of himself, clad in leather armor. A faint, upbeat jingle played in his head. This wasn't his life. This was… a video game. He tentatively reached out and touched his arm, feeling the rough texture of the leather. He knew, with a chilling certainty, that this was no dream.\n\n***\n\nPanic warred with a strange sense of detached curiosity. He stumbled out of bed, the floorboards creaking with an exaggerated sound effect. The door opened automatically as he approached, revealing a meticulously crafted village square bustling with strangely cheerful NPCs. A woman with impossibly large eyes and flowing blonde hair waved at him, her voice a synthesized melody. \"Welcome, hero! Are you ready to embark on your destiny?\" Arthur felt a surge of disbelief, quickly followed by a reluctant acceptance. He was trapped in Aethelgard, a world of quests and monsters, and apparently, he was the hero. He took a deep breath, the air smelling faintly of digital pine trees, and decided to at least try to figure out what a \"Sunstone\" was. He figured he might as well play along, at least until he figured out how to get out.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.32705190777778625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002044230350293219}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.1007833778858